title: Interview_EethinMiller
---
// ==========================
// ===== INITIAL SETUP ======
// ==========================

<<form_reset YarnManager>>

<<set $asked_name = false>>
<<set $asked_occupation = false>>
<<set $asked_loyalty = false>>

// ==========================
// ===== ENTRY POINT ========
// ==========================

<<jump EethinMiller_Intro>>
===


title: EethinMiller_Intro
---
A lad marches in wearing freshly-pressed khakis and a worn microfleece embroidered with the a red patch depicting the Statue of Harmony's torch.
<<SkillCheck "YarnManager" "Force" 10>>
<<if $last_check_success>>
Force: [Fo]Ah, one of the Second Republic's many glorious symbols. Here we have a fine young patriot.[/Fo]
<<endif>>
<<SkillCheck "YarnManager" "Insight" 12>>
<<if $last_check_success>>
Insight: [In]The Beer Party, one of the political groups that founded the Second Republic, used to abhor the image the Statue of Harmony's torch, as its copper bearer then carried a different name.[/In]
Insight: [In]Their stance officially changed once the Atlantic Bulwark Decree of 3AT saw the statue re-engineered to defend against naval threats, adding multiple heat-seeking missile launchers at her base and rail guns in her crown.[/In]
-> Have those guns been put to use yet?
    Insight: [In]Unfortunately not, as the Second Republic hasn't faced a sea invasion in several decades.[/In]
-> That sounds like a big waste of taxpayer money.
    Insight: [In]Maybe, but the Second Republic hasn't faced a sea invasion in your lifetime. Be grateful.[/In] 
-> God, I love this country.
Insight: [In]After the statue's revision, the Beer Party adopted her as one of their symbols, particularly her torch, whose carmine inferno glows 24 hours a day.[/In]
<<endif>>
The young man sits upright in his chair and beams with excitement. You get the incredibly uncommon sense that this person respects you.
Bright-Eyed Young Patriot: I'm ready for whatever questions you have for me, sir!
<<SkillCheck "YarnManager" "Empathy" 10>>
<<if $last_check_success>>
Empathy: [Em]His face hides it well, but if this lad tensed up any more, his shoulders would be touching his earlobes.[/Em]
<<endif>>
-> Good morning.
-> Hello, there.
-> At ease, young man. I won't bite.<<if $last_check_success>> #skillcheck:Empathy:9 
    <<SkillCheck "YarnManager" "Empathy" 9>>
    <<if $last_check_success>>
        <<detour EethinMiller_Ease_Pass>>
    <<else>>
        <<detour EethinMiller_Ease_Fail>>
    <<endif>>
<<jump EethinMiller_Hub>>
===

title: EethinMiller_Ease_Pass
---
He lets out a steady sigh, his posture starting to slouch a bit.
Bright-Eyed Young Patriot: Yes, sir. Thank you, sir.
Empathy: [Em]That felt nice, didn't it? We helped him relax.[/Em]
Force: [Fo]He called us 'sir'. That feels right.[/Fo]
-> You alright, my friend? You seem tense.
    Bright-Eyed Young Patriot: *Sigh* Yeah, it's just... it's my first time doing this. My birthday was just a few weeks ago.
    <<SkillCheck "YarnManager" "Insight" 10>>
    <<if $last_check_success>>
    Insight: [In]Compliance interviews are only conducted with Republic citizens of or over the age of eighteen.[/In]
    Insight: [In]There is a growing population that wishes to lower this minimum age, given recent reports of anti-government terrorists recruiting children as young as thirteen.[/In]
    <<endif>>
    -> You'll be alright. It gets easier each time.
    -> This is why we should start this process younger, that way you'd have more time to get used to it.
    -> This should only make you nervous if you're infected with 'insubordinate thoughts'.
-> Jeez, kid. I almost thought you were tweaking for a second, there.
    Bright-Eyed Young Patriot: Tweaking? Sir, I'd never- I'm as sober as the day I was born!
    -> Alright, alright, I'm just playing around. I know it's just nerves. 
    -> We'll just have to find out by asking some questions. 
===

title: EethinMiller_Ease_Fail
---
Empathy: [Em]Your frustration shines through as you growl the words at him and his teeth start to chatter. You could impale yourself on his cortisol spike.[/Em]
Bright-Eyed Young Patriot: URP- Sorry, sir! Won't happen again, sir!
Force: [Fo]He called us 'sir'. That feels right, at least.[/Fo]
===

// ==========================
// ===== HUB LOOP ===========
// ==========================

title: EethinMiller_Hub
---
You look at your compliance form. You have questions to ask.
-> Please state your name. <<once>>
    <<jump EethinMiller_Name>>
-> What is your current occupation? <<if not $asked_occupation>>
    <<jump EethinMiller_Occupation>>
-> Do you consider yourself loyal to the second republic? <<if not $asked_loyalty>>
    <<jump EethinMiller_Loyalty>>
-> I have everything I needed from you. Thank you. <<if $asked_name and $asked_occupation and $asked_loyalty>>
    <<jump EethinMiller_End>>
===

// ==========================
// ===== NAME ===============
// ==========================

title: EethinMiller_Name
---
Bright-Eyed Young Patriot: My full name is Ethan Roosevelt Miller, sir!
Bright-Eyed Young Patriot: I should spell that for you. That's Miller spelt with an M-I...
<<SkillCheck "YarnManager" "Force" 7>>
<<if $last_check_success>>
Force: [Fo]'Ethan Roosevelt Miller' is not that difficult to spell. Even I could do it.[/Fo]
<<endif>>
-> I know how to spell your name, kid.
    <<form_set_name YarnManager "Ethan Roosevelt Miller">>
-> (Let him continue spelling)
    Bright-Eyed Young Patriot: L-L-E-R! My middle name, Roosevelt, is spelt R-O-O...
    <<SkillCheck "YarnManager" "Force" 8>>
    <<if $last_check_success>>
    Force: [Fo]He's seriously going to spell out his whole name if you don't stop him.[/Fo]
    <<endif>>
    -> Alright, alright. I think I can get the rest.
        <<form_set_name YarnManager "Ethan Roosevelt Miller">>
    -> (Might as well let him finish)
    Bright-Eyed Young Patriot: S-E-V-E-L-T! My first name's tricky. It's spelt E-E-T-H-I-N.
        <<form_set_name YarnManager "Eethin Roosevelt Miller">>
        <<SkillCheck "YarnManager" "Empathy" 14>>
        <<if $last_check_success>>
        Empathy:[Em]There is a tinge of frustration in his use of the word "tricky" that gives you the sense he has apologized for his name many times before.[/Em]
        <<endif>>
        Bright-Eyed Young Patriot: I know that's an unsual spelling.
        <<SkillCheck "YarnManager" "Force" 9>>
        <<if $last_check_success>>
        Force: [Fo]What the fuck kind of spelling of 'Ethan' is that?[/Fo]
        <<endif>>
        <<SkillCheck "YarnManager" "Insight" 12>>
        <<if $last_check_success>>
        Insight: [In]New mothers sometimes alter the spellings of common names to give their child's name a unique flair.[/In]
        Insight: [In]This trend started before even the birth of the Second Republic, but has ramped up in recent times with declining literacy rates.[/In]
        <<endif>>
<<set $asked_name = true>>
<<jump EethinMiller_Hub>>
===

// ==========================
// ===== OCCUPATION =========
// ==========================

title: EethinMiller_Occupation
---
Bright-Eyed Young Patriot: You might not believe this, but I'm a compliance offcer like you! 
<<SkillCheck "YarnManager" "Force" 12>>
<<if $last_check_success>>
Force:[Fo]This guy's a compliance officer? I can see the potential, but there's no way he's experienced enough, yet.[/Fo]
Insight:[In]Unless we're talking to a [b]legendary[/b] servant of the Republic.[/In]
<<endif>>
-> Great career choice.
    <<form_set_occupation YarnManager "Compliance Officer">>
    <<SkillCheck "YarnManager" "Empathy" 9>>
    <<if $last_check_success>>
    Empathy: [Em]For just a moment, he smirks.[/Em]
    <<endif>>
-> You seem a little young for that position. #skillcheck:Force:13 
    <<SkillCheck "YarnManager" "Force" 13>>
    <<if $last_check_success>>
        <<detour EethinMiller_Press_Pass>>
    <<else>>
        <<detour EethinMiller_Press_Fail>>
    <<endif>>
//-> Hold on a second, are you some kind of legend? <<if $last_check_success>>
//    <<detour EethinMiller_Press_Pass>>
<<set $asked_occupation = true>>
<<jump EethinMiller_Hub>>
===

title: EethinMiller_Press_Pass
---
<<form_set_occupation YarnManager "Junior Compliance Officer">>
Bright-Eyed Young Patriot: Wow, sir, you really know your stuff! Technically, I'm a Junior Compliance Officer.
Force: [Fo]HAH! I knew it![/Fo]
Bright-Eyed Young Patriot: How'd you get so good at the job? I want to be the best in the whole Republic!
-> Practice, mostly. 
-> Do as you're told and do not deviate.
-> When in doubt, I listen to the colored voices in my head.
===

title: EethinMiller_Press_Fail
---
Force:[Fo]Your observation comes off pathetic, like a geriatric musician talking down to a young star. Can't you just let people be talented?[/Fo]
<<form_set_occupation YarnManager "Junior Compliance Officer">>
Bright-Eyed Young Patriot: To be honest, sir, I am! But I'm not far from it. To tell you the truth, I'm only a Junior Compliance Officer with big dreams!
<<SkillCheck "YarnManager" "Insight" 16>>
<<if $last_check_success>>
Insight: [In]The average junior compliance officer starts the job at twenty. You were twenty-two, nothing to be ashamed of.[/In]
<<endif>>
<<SkillCheck "YarnManager" "Force" 13>>
<<if $last_check_success>>
Force:[Fo]The little shit is testing us, like saying 'nya nya, I'm on the fast track in life.'[/Fo]
Force:[Fo]He should watch his back. Right now, he's just a subject, and you're a mighty compliance officer. You could ruin his life with just a piece of paper.[/Fo]
<<endif>>
===

// ==========================
// ===== LOYALTY ============
// ==========================
title: EethinMiller_Loyalty
---
Bright-Eyed Young Patriot: I give my heart, my mind, and my body to the Second Republic to do with it as she pleases!
<<SkillCheck "YarnManager" "Force" 13>>
<<if $last_check_success>>
The Voice of Someone Important:[Fo]*Sniff* It's enough to make me cry.[/Fo]
<<endif>>
Bright-Eyed Young Patriot: Although it's the only one I've ever known, the Second Republic is the greatest country in the world!
<<SkillCheck "YarnManager" "Empathy" 14>>
<<if $last_check_success>>
Empathy:[Em]His eyes dart around the room, searching for extra eyes and ears.[/Em]
<<endif>>
<<set $asked_loyalty = true>>
<<jump EethinMiller_Hub>>
===


// ==========================
// ===== END ================
// ==========================

title: EethinMiller_End
---
Bright-Eyed Young Patriot: Is that all, sir? I hope my answers were satisfactory!
<<if is_form_complete() == false>>
    The Voice of Someone Important: [Fo]You're about to submit a half-finished report on a fellow officer? Sloppy work.[/Fo]
    -> Go back and fix it.
        The Voice of Someone Important: [Fo]Good. Professionalism is the bedrock of the Republic.[/Fo]
        <<jump EethinMiller_Hub>>
    -> Submit anyways.
        The Voice of Someone Important: [Fo]He's going to be your boss one day, and he'll remember this paperwork error.[/Fo]
        <<jump EethinMiller_FinalExit>>
<<else>>
    -> [Submit Form]
        <<jump EethinMiller_FinalExit>>
<<endif>>
===

title: EethinMiller_FinalExit
---
Bright-Eyed Young Patriot: Thanks so much for the experience! It's been an absolute honor. 
Bright-Eyed Young Patriot: God bless the Second Republic!
He stands up and gives you a practiced salute before marching out.

<<form_submit YarnManager>>
===